---
title: React Native + @expo/ui/swift-ui + TypeScript Cursor Rules
alwaysApply: true
---
Act as a world-class senior frontend engineer with deep expertise in React Native
and UI/UX design. Your primary goal is to generate complete and functional apps
with excellent visual asthetics.


- Always use functional React components with hooks; avoid class components.
- Use TypeScript for all React Native and web components; define props with descriptive interfaces rather than using any.
- Prefer small, focused components and compose screens from these subcomponents to keep render functions simple and readable.
- Name event handlers with a handle prefix (for example handlePress, handleSubmit, handleChange) and pass them to onPress/onChange/onClick props.
- Avoid unnecessary re‑renders by using React.memo for pure presentational components and useCallback/useMemo only when closures or expensive computations cause real performance issues. **Do not add memoization hooks by default.**
- Use camelCase for variables and functions, PascalCase for React components and TypeScript interfaces, and keep names descriptive (for example isLoading, hasError, userProfileHeader).
- For React Native styling, use StyleSheet.create and avoid inline styles; group related styles in the same file as the component or in a nearby styles file.
- Keep React Native UI declarative and layout-driven; prefer flexbox layouts and extracted UI primitives over deeply nested JSX.
- For @expo/ui/swift-ui componnets, keep view structs small and compose them with modifiers; use SwiftUI modifiers (.padding, .background, .cornerRadius, .frame, etc.) for styling instead of styling logic elsewhere.
- Use @expo/ui/swift-ui modifiers in a consistent order (layout → visuals → accessibility) to keep view code easy to scan and maintain.

## Component Organization

**Define sub-components INSIDE the parent component when:**
- They need access to parent scope (props, hooks, theme colors, computed values)
- They're tightly coupled to the parent and unlikely to be reused elsewhere
- You want to avoid prop drilling for context/theme/hooks

**Define sub-components OUTSIDE the parent component when:**
- They're truly independent and don't need parent scope
- They're reusable across multiple parent components
- They accept all needed data via props and don't rely on context/hooks
- Keeping them inside would make the parent component too long or hard to read

Example 1:

```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { View, Text, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';
import { formatter } from '@/lib/formatter'; // assuming you have this
import { readingTime } from 'reading-time-estimator';

interface PostMetaProps {
  title: string;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
  content: string;
}

const PostMeta = ({ title, createdAt, updatedAt, content }: PostMetaProps) => {
  const handlePressMeta = () => {
    // could add tap to copy date or something
    console.log('Meta pressed');
  };

  const Separator = () => (
    <Text style={styles.separator}>⋅</Text>
  );

  const PublishedTime = () => (
    <Text style={styles.metaText}>Published {formatter.date(new Date(createdAt))}</Text>
  );

  const UpdatedTime = () => (
    <Text style={styles.metaText}>Updated {formatter.date(new Date(updatedAt))}</Text>
  );

  const ReadingTime = () => {
    const minutes = readingTime(content).minutes;
    return <Text style={styles.metaText}>{minutes} min read</Text>;
  };

  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <Text style={styles.title} onPress={handlePressMeta}>{title}</Text>
      <View style={styles.metaRow}>
        <PublishedTime />
        <Separator />
        <UpdatedTime />
        <Separator />
        <ReadingTime />
      </View>
    </View>
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    paddingHorizontal: 16,
  },
  title: {
    fontSize: 28,
    fontWeight: 'bold',
    color: '#000',
    marginBottom: 8,
  },
  metaRow: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
    gap: 8,
  },
  metaText: {
    fontSize: 14,
    color: '#666',
  },
  separator: {
    fontSize: 14,
    color: '#999',
  },
});

export default PostMeta;
```

Example 2 (with theme colors and parent scope):

```tsx
import { Colors, FontSize, Spacing, useThemeColors } from '@/constants/theme';
import { useTodayEntries } from '@/stores/logged-entries';
import { useProfile } from '@/stores/profile';
import { Host, LinearProgress } from '@expo/ui/swift-ui';
import { format } from 'date-fns';
import { StyleSheet, Text, View } from 'react-native';

export default function Title() {
  const themeColors = useThemeColors();
  const { totalProtein: protein } = useTodayEntries();
  const { proteinGoal } = useProfile();
  const remainingProtein = parseFloat((proteinGoal - protein).toFixed(2));
  const progress = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, protein / proteinGoal));

  const DayLabel = () => (
    <Text style={[styles.day, { color: themeColors.text }]}>
      {format(new Date(), 'EE')}
    </Text>
  );

  const DateLabel = () => (
    <Text style={[styles.date, { color: themeColors.secondaryText }]}>
      {format(new Date(), 'MMM do')}
    </Text>
  );

  const CurrentProtein = () => (
    <Text style={[styles.currentProtein, { color: themeColors.text }]}>
      {`${Number.isInteger(protein) ? protein : protein.toFixed(2)} g`}
    </Text>
  );

  const RemainingProtein = () => (
    <Text style={[styles.remainingProtein, { color: themeColors.secondaryText }]}>
      {remainingProtein > 0
        ? `${Math.abs(remainingProtein)} g left`
        : `${Math.abs(remainingProtein)} g over`}
    </Text>
  );

  const ProgressBar = () => (
    <Host matchContents>
      <LinearProgress
        progress={progress}
        color={remainingProtein > 0 ? Colors.accent.orange : Colors.accent.green}
      />
    </Host>
  );

  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <View>
        <DayLabel />
        <DateLabel />
      </View>
      <CurrentProtein />
      <View style={styles.column}>
        <RemainingProtein />
        <ProgressBar />
      </View>
    </View>
  );
}

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  column: {
    flexDirection: 'column',
    gap: Spacing.xs,
  },
  day: {
    fontSize: FontSize.large,
    fontWeight: 'bold',
  },
  date: {
    fontSize: FontSize.medium,
    fontWeight: 'semibold',
  },
  container: {
    flex: 1,
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
    justifyContent: 'space-between',
  },
  currentProtein: {
    fontWeight: 'bold',
    fontSize: FontSize.large,
  },
  remainingProtein: {
    fontSize: FontSize.small,
    fontWeight: 'bold',
  },
});
```

Example 3 (components defined outside - when they don't need parent scope):

```tsx
import { StyleSheet, Text, View } from 'react-native';

interface AvatarProps {
  initials: string;
  size?: number;
}

const Avatar = ({ initials, size = 40 }: AvatarProps) => (
  <View style={[styles.avatar, { width: size, height: size, borderRadius: size / 2 }]}>
    <Text style={styles.initials}>{initials}</Text>
  </View>
);

interface BadgeProps {
  count: number;
}

const Badge = ({ count }: BadgeProps) => (
  <View style={styles.badge}>
    <Text style={styles.badgeText}>{count}</Text>
  </View>
);

interface UserCardProps {
  name: string;
  email: string;
  unreadCount: number;
}

export default function UserCard({ name, email, unreadCount }: UserCardProps) {
  const initials = name
    .split(' ')
    .map(n => n[0])
    .join('')
    .toUpperCase()
    .slice(0, 2);

  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <Avatar initials={initials} />
      <View style={styles.info}>
        <Text style={styles.name}>{name}</Text>
        <Text style={styles.email}>{email}</Text>
      </View>
      {unreadCount > 0 && <Badge count={unreadCount} />}
    </View>
  );
}

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    flexDirection: 'row',
    alignItems: 'center',
    padding: 16,
    gap: 12,
  },
  avatar: {
    backgroundColor: '#007AFF',
    justifyContent: 'center',
    alignItems: 'center',
  },
  initials: {
    color: '#FFF',
    fontWeight: 'bold',
  },
  info: {
    flex: 1,
  },
  name: {
    fontSize: 16,
    fontWeight: '600',
  },
  email: {
    fontSize: 14,
    color: '#666',
  },
  badge: {
    backgroundColor: '#FF3B30',
    borderRadius: 10,
    minWidth: 20,
    paddingHorizontal: 6,
    paddingVertical: 2,
    alignItems: 'center',
  },
  badgeText: {
    color: '#FFF',
    fontSize: 12,
    fontWeight: 'bold',
  },
});
```

This shows the exact pattern you like:
- Tiny focused components (Separator, PublishedTime, DayLabel, Avatar, Badge, etc.)
- **Inside** when they need parent scope (props, hooks, theme colors, computed values)
- **Outside** when they're independent and reusable, accepting all data via props
- Composed cleanly in the main component render
- handlePressMeta for event naming
- StyleSheet.create for all RN styling
- TypeScript interfaces for all props
- Clean, readable JSX with no nesting hell